<title>GERMANY: Italy called monetary committee meeting - source.</title>
<headline>Italy called monetary committee meeting - source.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian government has requested that a meeting of the European Union monetary committee be called for Saturday, a senior source told Reuters on the fringes of the European Banking Congress.</p>
<p>&quot;The Italians have requested a meeting of the monetary committee for tomorrow,&quot; the source, who declined to be identified, said.</p>
<p>The EU monetary committee is empowered to decide on membership of Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism. Italy's Treasury Minister, Carlo Azeglio Ciampi, said earlier today that he wanted to take the lira back into the ERM this month.</p>
</text>
